📅 Week 1: Data Acquisition, Cleaning & Introduction to Power BI

During the first week, the primary focus was on collecting, understanding, and preparing the IT Support Ticket dataset sourced from an internal ticketing system. The dataset was loaded and explored to identify column types, relationships, and key attributes such as ticket priority, issue category, timestamps, and resolution status.

We defined important performance metrics like Resolution Time, Response Efficiency, and Priority Distribution, which will be used to evaluate support performance in later stages.

A significant part of this week was dedicated to data cleaning and preprocessing. Missing, null, and inconsistent values were identified and handled appropriately to ensure data quality. New features were engineered, such as Resolution_Time (calculated as the difference between resolution date and ticket creation date). Additionally, the Similarity_Level field was grouped into meaningful performance buckets to simplify analysis.

We also began working with Power BI, gaining an understanding of its interface and capabilities for data visualization. Using Power Query, the dataset was transformed by:

Removing duplicates and irrelevant columns
Handling missing values
Changing data types
Creating calculated columns
Preparing the dataset for analysis and reporting

Categorical fields were encoded and structured properly to support future tasks like clustering, dashboard creation, and advanced analytics.

This week established a strong foundation by ensuring clean, structured, and analysis-ready data, along with an introduction to visualization tools that will be used in the upcoming weeks.
